{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nprobe-rebar.sh accumulated stale assertions (08ce: 3 stale asserts against removed flags/keysets). Its missing 'set -e' is DELIBERATE harness design (continue past failures, report all) — a naive port or hardening pass would break it.\n\n## Approach\nPort to a Python probe harness (scripts/probe_rebar.py) preserving the continue-on-failure design (collect results, report all, exit non-zero if any failed — the same contract, now explicit). Assertion-parity review required: every current assertion enumerated and carried over or retired with a reason (the 08ce class came from silent drift). Do NOT add set -e semantics.\n\nShell deletion and consumer re-pointing happen in the SAME change, after the side-by-side parity run: every consumer that hard-wires the shell path is re-pointed to the Python entry point in this change, so CI and the anti-rot gate track the new harness atomically.\n\n## Scope\n- scripts/probe-rebar.sh -> scripts/probe_rebar.py (port + delete shell)\n- Consumers re-pointed in the same change (enumerated by grep for 'probe-rebar'):\n  - .github/workflows/test.yml:128 — 'bash scripts/probe-rebar.sh </dev/null' -> python invocation\n  - .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:209 — same re-point\n  - .github/workflows/external-integration.yml:54 — comment mentioning the path; update wording\n  - tests/unit/test_probe_wired_into_ci.py — _PROBE_JOBS asserts substring 'scripts/probe-rebar.sh' in golden-path jobs; update the pinned substring to the Python entry point so the anti-rot gate keeps guarding\n  - docs/releasing.md:401,405,407 — invocation examples -> Python equivalents\n  - CHANGELOG.md + docs/experiments corpus jsonl are historical records — NOT touched.\n- Assertion inventory table in the change description (commit message).\n\n## Testing\nSelf-test: inject one failing probe -> harness continues, reports it, exits non-zero. Parity: run both harnesses against the same build before deletion, identical pass/fail verdict per assertion. tests/unit/test_probe_wired_into_ci.py green against the updated substring.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Python harness replaces the shell probe with continue-on-failure preserved.\n- [x] Assertion-parity table: every shell assertion mapped to ported/retired-with-reason.\n- [x] Side-by-side run shows identical verdicts; shell deleted in the same change with ALL enumerated consumers (workflows, anti-rot test, docs) re-pointed to the Python entry point."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785768274049739001,"uuid":"43c49d77-a62c-49c5-bef0-31d2fdc16705"}